  "responseTimeMs": 19710,
  "answer": "### Short Answer\nYes, Expanded Withholding Tax (EWT) is required on payments to a VAT-registered law firm. This is in accordance with the provisions of the National Internal Revenue Code (NIRC).\n\n### Interpretation\n\n### Practical Meaning\nFor businesses engaging the services of a VAT-registered law firm, it is essential to account for EWT in their payment processes. This means that when making payments, the business must withhold the specified EWT rate from the total amount due to the law firm and remit this withheld amount to the BIR. Failure to comply with this requirement may result in penalties and interest for the withholding agent.",
